Z||000000||Springtyme||10-16-2001||09:53 AM||||Driving home from work last night I was thinking to myself "Well, the good thing is I will always know if any of my lights go out. The head lights pop up, and I can see the third brake light on the deck lid." So I pull in the driveway of the house that I'm watching their dog (actually it's eric's parents house) and go inside. I sit down with him and watch a little bit of TV, then we both go to leave. I hop in my car, start it up, see what I can do about getting a little bit of heat. Then I put it in reverse and back outta the driveway. I start to go down the street and I realize "Duh, I need lights" so I pop them up. <P>  "Uth oh..." put them back down, put them up again. "Oh sh!t" so I pull over and try to figure out why the heck they aren't workin. On the same note, I know nothing about cars except how to drive them and crack them up. So I wait about 2 minutes for when I know Eric will be home, and call him from my cell phone and ask him to come back and help me. <P>  He comes back, tells me there's nothing he can do about it anymore that night, but he'll fix it for me today. However, I work until 8:30 tonight and it's gonna be dark by the time I get out of work, so I have to drive my Beretta to and from work. I'm not very happy about it. =( The only up side is I can still drive my Fiero around this afternoon before I go into work.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Raydar||10-16-2001||11:00 AM||||If they don't come up, flip the switch off and back on quickly. My formula does this. <BR>Should be either the controller or the switch causing the problem.  The controller should  be inside the left front fender, in front of the wheelwell liner.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Springtyme||10-16-2001||11:02 AM||||Oh they came up, thats not the problem. The problem is the lights don't work, as in, they don't shine or light up. =( I should really be driving it around now but I'm hooked on ebay =)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||10-16-2001||12:11 PM||||Sounds like a bad fuse link at the junction block by the battery (85 & up) or switch (built in circuit breaker).<BR>Do you have dash lights?||||reg||1
