Z||000005||Eric_PA||10-16-2001||05:36 PM||||Found the problem, but still can't beleive it. Both of the low elements in the head lights burned out at the same time.<BR>???? voltage spike ????<BR>Can get away with driving on the high setting for now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Eric<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000006||StuGood||10-16-2001||06:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric_PA:<BR><B>...still can't beleive it. Both of the low elements in the head lights burned out at the same time.  Eric</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I can.  I've got 3 old headlamps in a box, and the "dim" element's burned out in all of them.  Can't bring myself to toss them out, 'cause I know the "bright" elements are still good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">!  <P>Of course, I assume the reason "dims" tend to burn out first, is because they see more usage.  What I <B>don't</B> understand is, how do they know to burn out the night before I go a long-distance trip?  Happened to me this last weekend... just one side burned out, though.<P>Glad the problem turned out to be a simple one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <BR>||||reg||3
